🚽 Test case: round-14 review finding #2 -- infer_expression_abi_type()
🚽 claims to report the type a native-ABI marshalling call will actually
🚽 produce, but previously left VAR_ENUM untouched (it only normalized
🚽 VAR_CHAR-related shapes). ast_expr_to_stdrot_value() (stdrot.c) has no
🚽 STDROT_ENUM -- StdrotType has no such member -- so an enum-typed
🚽 expression always marshals as STDROT_INT, the same as a bare int.
🚽 identity<T>(T)'s static T (infer_expression_type()'s NODE_FUNC_CALL case,
🚽 via infer_expression_abi_type() on the identity argument) must report
🚽 VAR_INT for an enum argument to match, not VAR_ENUM. Deliberately uses an
🚽 enum VARIABLE, not a bare enum constant -- find_global_enum_constant()
🚽 already reports a constant's type as plain int, which would hide this
🚽 gap entirely.
gyatt Color {
    RED,
    GREEN,
    BLUE
};

skibidi main {
    gyatt Color favorite = GREEN;
    rizz r = identity(favorite);
    yapping("%d", r);
    bussin 0;
}
